\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{The overlap of the Wilson kernel}
\date{2026-11-23}

\p{Take the [Wilson operator](fdip-009U) at trivial links with
#{a>0}, #{c_W=a/2}, and periods #{N_j\ge3}. Shift its mass by
putting #{K=D_{W,a,U}-a^{-1}\bbI}. In any dimension #{n\ge1}
let #{\Gamma} be a site-independent self-adjoint grading on
#{S\otimes F} anticommuting with every represented generator.
With #{f,m} from \ref{fdip-0144}, write
#{A=\sum_j f_j(r)(\varepsilon_j^S\otimes\bbI_F)}. The block is
#{K(p)=(m(r)-a^{-1})\bbI+\ui A}. Conjugation by #{\Gamma} negates #{A}, so
#{\Gamma K(p)\Gamma=K(p)^\dagger} and
##{\begin{aligned}
(\Gamma K(p))^2&=K(p)^\dagger K(p)=b(r)^2\bbI,\\
b(r)&=\sqrt{|f(r)|^2+(m(r)-a^{-1})^2}.
\end{aligned}}
At a grid corner with #{h} coordinates equal to #{\pi},
#{m(r)=2h/a}. Thus #{m(r)-a^{-1}=(2h-1)/a} is nonzero.
Away from the corners #{f(r)\ne0}, so every #{b(r)>0}.}

\p{On each block the eigenvalues of the Hermitian #{\Gamma K(p)}
belong to #{\{-b(r),b(r)\}}. Its sign grading is
#{\Gamma_K(p)=\Gamma K(p)/b(r)}. Hence the overlap formula of
\ref{fdip-014D} gives
##{D_K(p)=a^{-1}\left(\bbI+\frac{K(p)}{b(r)}\right).}
Its vector part is #{f(r)/(ab(r))}. The only zero block is at
the origin, where the mass becomes #{0}. The other sampled
corners have mass #{2a^{-1}}. At a zero vertex each of the
other values in an incident simplex is scaled by a positive
factor. The spanned cone and the sign of its determinant are
preserved, so each local degree agrees with \ref{fdip-0142}.
The origin has degree #{1}.}

\p{More explicitly, write #{d_i=1/(ab(r_i))} at the vertices
of any grid simplex. Given barycentric weights #{\lambda_i} for
the rescaled map, put
##{\mu_i=\frac{d_i\lambda_i}{\sum_jd_j\lambda_j}.}
The rescaled interpolated vector is #{\sum_jd_j\lambda_j}
times the original interpolated vector at #{\mu}. This
correspondence preserves faces and is invertible by the same
formula with reciprocal factors. Thus it carries rescaled zeros
to original zeros, possibly at different barycentric positions.
The equal vertex degrees and \ref{fdip-0140} give equal aggregate
off-grid degrees.}

\p{The first represented generator conjugates #{\Gamma} to
#{-\Gamma}, and #{\Gamma} conjugates #{\Gamma A} to
#{-\Gamma A}. Both traces vanish, so
#{\Gamma_K(p)=((m(r)-a^{-1})\Gamma+\ui\Gamma A)/b(r)}
has trace zero on every block. The full #{\Gamma} also has
trace zero, and \ref{fdip-014D} gives #{\sdim\ker D_K=0}.
Directly the whole constant block survives and the first generator
exchanges its two grading spaces. In even dimension this includes
the volume grading #{C}.}
